# For Developers

Version 4.0.0 adds the following platforms:
- Bungee
- Spigot

_(After this I will probably not release major releases this frequently because I don't have as many platforms to implement)_
Also, of course, the Spigot and Bungee versions will be limited a lot, and don't expect any Adventure stuff to work on there. It's mostly there just to chill out. The only reason to use the Spigot version is that it has a small inventory library, but it doesn't even have the NoteMaker because I couldn't find a way to edit an item's PDC

## Fabric and Velocity changes

The configuration system is now on another dependency, which it now gives you as an API, so that means you'll need to change the packages:
- `net.chamosmp.sqdlib.<platform>.config` to `com.sqdstudios.bukkit.configuration`


## Spigot and Paper features

Spigot and Paper also now have small economy utilities for Vault with NaN and other checks to make sure that sneaky transaction didn't give you NaN amount of money (Which NaN amount of money is a lot btw)

## Core Changes

Who would like some new useless annotation? Me, me! We added a `Requires` annotation which shows what things a class, package, etc. needs to be used

We also added a `Random` class whose only function is to choose a random `T` from a list of `T`s and their chances

There might be more changes, but have fun developing, my friends!

### Migrating to v4

You'll first need to replace every instance of `net.chamosmp` with `com.sqdstudios` (And in the dependency too)

If you're migrating from even older versions like v2, you should delete the packages that are not found and make your
IDE suggest them to you because they're undocumented

