# For fabric users

If you're a user of a fabric mod that needs this, you can download it from the assets. I'm looking to add it to Modrinth soon

# For Developers

### Things to look out for

This version changes some packages, so don't worry if you get errors! You should just delete the imports and let it auto-complete them for you.

## Velocity

Make it not experimental

## Fabric

You can now use the logger without needing to initiate it, and you can use MiniMessage in it now. Yayy!

## Paper

Paper now has some new utilities which may be useful:

- NoteMaker
   - Create notes more easily. If you don't know what notes are, see [this](https://sqd-studios.github.io/docs/chamoitemskins/administration/introduction/understanding/#notes)
- chamogui
   - A small GUI library based on the Bukkit inventory system instead of MenuType. I don't really recommend trying this while it is undocumented. An example of this being used can be found in ChamoItemSkins
- DebugLogger
   - A logger which only logs if debug is enabled (Which it finds through the config (the key is `debug: true`))

This should be it for Paper. I also have planned something for more advanced dialogs, so stay tuned

## Core

Make the annotation retention from runtime to source

